    "https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Program-Assistant---Arts--Design---Communication_JR00000972": {
      "title": "Program Assistant - Arts, Design & Communication",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nChatham University welcomes your interest in employment opportunities and encourages you to review open positions. Please note that Chatham does not accept unsolicited applications. Program Assistant Chatham University is seeking a detail-oriented Program Assistant to join the Arts, Design and Communications department. Under limited supervision, provide high level support in areas of communications, fiscal oversight, database development and management, report preparation, event planning, and logistics.  This position is an integral part of the day-to-day operations of the Arts, Design & Communication department. The ideal candidate is enthusiastic, invested, and trustworthy with a preference for a fast paced and ever-evolving work culture. Responsibilities: Provide quality information, direction, and assistance to faculty and staff as well as incoming, currently enrolled students, and alumni. Manage timelines, priorities and multi-task while working independently or with limited supervision. Prepare and monitor faculty contracts as well as other department correspondence as needed. Order supplies for the department. Monitor and regularly balance departmental budget. Record meeting minutes and distribute to meeting attendees. Generate standard and custom-request reports on a regular and as-needed basis. Assist with scheduling meetings, classes, events, field trips, transportation, etc. Facilitate mail distribution and collection. Assist with Admissions activities such as planning a student visit to the department. Compile aggregate data and format reports that are utilized for departmental reports. Create and manage a database of students, courses, schedules, faculty and alumni. Correspond with students in a professional and effective manner. Post information to social media and manage social media sites. Event planning, including communicating updated and timely information, budget, location negotiations, dining, and audiovisual equipment arrangements. Disseminate electronic surveys and other data collection tools and compile results of course, program, and alumni surveys. Qualifications: Minimum of Associate Degree, Bachelor’s Degree preferred. Strong communication skills, written skills, and computer skills. Strong organizational skills. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications. Proficiency in Adobe applications is preferred.                      Ability to communicate task status and completion daily. Ability to interact and work well with faculty, students, alumni, and colleagues. Proven track record in administrative accuracy and quality monitoring. Salary Range :   $34,600-$39,350. 35 -hour work week. Exact compensation based on candidate skills and experience.   How to Apply:  Applications accepted only via www.chatham.edu/careers  (direct link is https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Program-Assistant---Arts--Design---Communication_JR00000972 ) and follow the instructions to complete the application process. To ensure full consideration, please include:  Cover Letter outlining your qualifications for the position  Curriculum Vitae or Resume  Contact information for three professional references  All application materials should be uploaded at the same time at the time of application. The system will not allow applicants to make edits to their applications after submission. Chatham University strives to promote a campus environment that understands and embraces multiculturalism while increasing individuals' intercultural competence. We actively work to build and sustain a diverse and culturally vibrant campus, which promotes employee and student success and retention.   Chatham University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity, inclusion, and equity. Chatham University does not discriminate on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, age, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital or family status, political affiliation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law."
