    "https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Assistant-Women-s-Wrestling-Coach_JR00000939": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nChatham University welcomes your interest in employment opportunities and encourages you to review open positions. Please note that Chatham does not accept unsolicited applications. Assistant Women’s Wrestling Coach Chatham University is seeking a dedicated and enthusiastic Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach to support all aspects of its NCAA Division III Women's Wrestling Program, a member of the Presidents' Athletic Conference (PAC). This position offers an excellent opportunity to help build a competitive program while fostering the academic, athletic, and personal development of student-athletes. The Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach will assist the Head Women's Wrestling Coach in the daily operation of the wrestling program. Responsibilities include recruiting prospective student-athletes, supporting coaching and player development, assisting with program administration, and ensuring compliance with NCAA Division III, PAC, and University regulations. The successful candidate will serve as a positive role model and ambassador for Chatham University and its athletics programs. Duties and Responsibilities: Assist in planning, organizing, implementing, and evaluating recruiting efforts to attract qualified student-athletes. Support athletic planning, program development, and the assessment of student-athlete performance, retention, personal growth, and leadership development. Assist with practice planning, competition preparation, and day-to-day program operations. Help oversee and manage program resources and equipment. Support campus initiatives and assist in coordinating athletic events that enhance campus engagement and school spirit. Ensure compliance with all Chatham University, NCAA Division III, and Presidents' Athletic Conference (PAC) rules, regulations, and policies. Represent the Women's Wrestling program at on-campus events, admissions programs, and University functions. Represent the program at recruiting events, tournaments, and high school competitions. Promote a culture of sportsmanship, integrity, academic achievement, and personal responsibility. Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Women's Wrestling Coach. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required. Excellent leadership skills and strong character. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as required. Commitment to the educational mission of NCAA Division III athletics. How to Apply:  Applications accepted only via www.chatham.edu/careers  (direct link is https://chatham.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/ChathamUniversity/job/Pittsburgh-PA/Assistant-Women-s-Wrestling-Coach_JR00000939 ) and follow the instructions to complete the application process. To ensure full consideration, please include:  Cover Letter outlining your qualifications for the position  Curriculum Vitae or Resume  Contact information for three professional references  All application materials should be uploaded at the same time at the time of application. The system will not allow applicants to make edits to their applications after submission. Chatham University strives to promote a campus environment that understands and embraces multiculturalism while increasing individuals' intercultural competence. We actively work to build and sustain a diverse and culturally vibrant campus, which promotes employee and student success and retention.   Chatham University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity, inclusion, and equity. Chatham University does not discriminate on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, age, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital or family status, political affiliation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law."
